meta {
  name: Initialize with Saved State
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/init
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "{{linkedinEmail}}"
  }
}

docs {
  # Initialize Browser with Saved State
  
  This endpoint initializes a new browser session and attempts to restore
  saved browser state (cookies, localStorage, sessionStorage) if available.
  
  ## Request Body
  - `email` (optional): Email address to identify saved browser state
  
  ## Response
  - `sessionId`: Unique session identifier
  - `sessionRestored`: Boolean indicating if saved state was restored
  - `message`: Status message
  
  ## Usage
  
  ### First Time (No Saved State)
  If no saved state exists for the email, a fresh browser session is created.
  You'll need to call the login endpoint next.
  
  ### Subsequent Times (With Saved State)
  If saved state exists and is valid:
  - Browser state is restored automatically
  - Session is marked as authenticated
  - Message monitoring starts automatically
  - You can skip the login step entirely!
  
  ## Benefits
  - Skip login process
  - Avoid CAPTCHA challenges
  - Faster initialization
  - Persistent sessions across API restarts
}
